    "body": "- [x] *Encryption at the level of Orbeon Forms* – Encryption and decryption will happen at the level of Orbeon Forms, so the values of the fields marked as \"to be encrypted\" will never be sent to the database (let alone stored by the database).\r\n- [x] *Form data* – When the value of a field is encrypted, in the form data the containing element will have the attribute `encrypted=\"true\"`.\r\n- [x] *Form Builder UI* – The \"Control Settings\" dialog will have a checkbox allowing form authors to mark a field for encryption.\r\n- [x] *Persistence proxy* – The Form Runner \"front-end\" will always see unencrypted data, and it is up to the persistence proxy to encrypt and decrypt data as needed.  When saving data, the persistence proxy will encrypt all fields marked as \"to be encrypted\" in the form definition before passing the form data to a specific implementation of the persistence API. Conversely, when reading data, it will decrypt all the fields that have the attribute `encrypted=\"true\"`.\r\n- [x] *Form Runner homepage in admin mode* – On this page, admins will be able to select a form definition and trigger data re-encryption for that form. Re-encryption will use the search API to get a list of all the form data, and for each form data, will read it, encrypt or decrypt fields according to the form definition, and if any change is needed, will write the form data back.\r\n* *Limitations* – On summary pages, encrypted fields won't be included in the free text search, and field search for encrypted fields will only be able to do exact matches.\r\n* *Out of scope* – The ability to change a key is out of scope for this request for enhancement.\r\n\r\n[+1 from customer](https://3.basecamp.com/3600924/buckets/1966718/messages/964223126#__recording_971644821)",
